1
00:03:26,896 --> 00:03:32,896
Growing up is a beast.

2
00:06:53,793 --> 00:06:59,793
Turning Red is a animation, family, comedy film directed by Domee Shi.

3
00:10:20,689 --> 00:10:26,689
Thirteen-year-old Mei is experiencing the awkwardness of being a teenager with a twist
– when she gets too excited, she transforms into a giant red panda.

4
00:13:47,586 --> 00:13:53,586
Meilin Lee (voice), played by Rosalie Chiang.

5
00:17:14,482 --> 00:17:20,482
Ming (voice), played by Sandra Oh.

6
00:20:41,379 --> 00:20:47,379
Miriam (voice), played by Ava Morse.

7
00:24:08,275 --> 00:24:14,275
Abby (voice), played by Hyein Park.

8
00:27:35,172 --> 00:27:41,172
Priya (voice), played by Maitreyi Ramakrishnan.

9
00:31:02,068 --> 00:31:08,068
Jin Lee (voice), played by Orion Lee.

10
00:34:28,965 --> 00:34:34,965
Turning Red is a 2022 American animated coming-of-age fantasy comedy-drama film
produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures.

11
00:37:55,862 --> 00:38:01,862
It was directed by Domee Shi and produced by Lindsey Collins, from a screenplay
written by Shi and Julia Cho, and a story by Shi, Cho, and Sarah Streicher.

12
00:41:22,758 --> 00:41:28,758
The film marks the first Pixar feature film solely directed by a woman.

13
00:44:49,655 --> 00:44:55,655
It stars the voices of Rosalie Chiang, Sandra Oh, Ava Morse,
Hyein Park, Maitreyi Ramakrishnan, and Orion Lee.

14
00:48:16,551 --> 00:48:22,551
Set in Toronto, Ontario in 2002, the film follows Meilin "Mei" Lee (Chiang), a 13-year-old Chinese-Canadian student who
transforms into a giant red panda when she experiences any strong emotion, due to a hereditary curse.

15
00:51:43,448 --> 00:51:49,448
Shi, who previously directed the short film Bao (2018), developed the
film based on her experiences growing up in Toronto.

16
00:55:10,344 --> 00:55:16,344
She pitched three concepts, including Turning Red, to Pixar in October 2017.

17
00:58:37,241 --> 00:58:43,241
Development began in May 2018 when Shi was announced as writer and director of a full-length film; several Pixar
animators visited locations around Northern California gathering inspiration and visual references.

18
01:02:04,137 --> 01:02:10,137
The design and animation were inspired by anime works.

19
01:05:31,034 --> 01:05:37,034
To capture these anime influences, hand-drawn 2D animated
effects were added atop Pixar's 3D animation.

20
01:08:57,931 --> 01:09:03,931
Development on Turning Red lasted for four years, on an approximate $175
million budget, becoming the fastest production for a Pixar film.

21
01:12:24,827 --> 01:12:30,827
Ludwig Göransson composed the film's musical score for his first animated film, with
Billie Eilish and Finneas O'Connell writing original songs for the film.

22
01:15:51,724 --> 01:15:57,724
Turning Red was first shown in London at Everyman Borough Yards on February 21, 2022, as a special screening, in
Toronto at TIFF Bell Lightbox on March 8, and at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on March 1.

23
01:19:18,620 --> 01:19:24,620
Originally planned for a worldwide theatrical release, plans
were changed due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

24
01:22:45,517 --> 01:22:51,517
The film was released on March 11, 2022, on the Disney+ streaming service and was released
theatrically in most countries without the streaming service, grossing over $21 million.

25
01:26:12,413 --> 01:26:18,413
It was paired with the short film Kitbull for its theatrical release in the
United States and the United Kingdom on February 9, 2024.

26
01:29:39,310 --> 01:29:45,310
Turning Red received critical acclaim and was nominated for Best Animated
Feature at the 95th Academy Awards, among numerous other accolades.

27
01:33:06,206 --> 01:33:12,206
The film explores themes of friendship, canada, concert, temple, shapeshifting.

28
01:36:33,103 --> 01:36:39,103
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
